venv
.venv

# Secrets and real data that a build must never bake into the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything left behind by running the
# app locally travels into the image - which is a distributable artifact.
# The database was already excluded above; these are the rest of what the
# app writes beside it:
#
# - .session_secret / .setup_token_hash: generated secrets. At runtime the
#   app reads them from DATA_DIR (/data), never from /app, so a copy in the
#   image is useless to the app and useful only to whoever has the image.
# - backups/: the preference CSV backups (lib/preferencesBackup.ts), one
#   per person per period, with what each of them actually filled in.
# - .test-data/: the test database and its own backups.
# - data/: the default DATA_DIR from docker-compose.yml, and the case that
#   matters most - an operator building the image on the machine the app
#   has been running on has a full database and everyone's preference CSVs
#   sitting right there. It is a bind-mount target, so whatever ends up in
#   the image at that path is shadowed at runtime regardless.
#
# The ** variants are not redundant: Docker matches these against the whole
# relative path and a plain * never crosses a /, so `*.db*` alone does not
# match `data/rooster.db`, and a custom DATA_DIR puts them somewhere else
# again.
.session_secret
.setup_token_hash
data
backups
**/backups
**/*.db*
**/.session_secret
**/.setup_token_hash
.test-data
coverage
